"DFA states q0..q4, accepting {q3,q4}; q0:0→q1,1→q2; q1,q2:0→q3,1→q4; q3,q4:0→q3,1→q4. Partitions: {q0,q1,q2},{q3,q4} → {q0},{q1,q2},{q3,q4}. Minimal DFA has 3 states (strings of length ≥2).",
["Step 1: remove unreachable states.","Step 2: start with partition {F, Q−F}.","Step 3: refine groups whose members go to different groups on some symbol.","Step 4: stop when no change; each group becomes one state.","Myhill–Nerode: number of equivalence classes = minimal DFA size.","Table-filling algorithm marks distinguishable pairs."],
